      "updated": 1786609783335,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design a ecommerce app",
      "fontSize": 40.38419000915383,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design a ecommerce app",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "aPYEzYb2m6zrcpN6x_8t1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1093.6310964156487,
      "y": 4527.577964884063,
      "width": 817.0592041015625,
      "height": 1850,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b8S",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1689318430,
      "version": 3457,
      "versionNonce": 2136694842,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786601261400,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Functional Requirements\n    - user should be able to search products based on name, description, title\n    - user should be able to view the details of a product .\n    - user should be able to select the product quantity and add to cart\n    - user should be able to reserve stock at checkout (hold N min) then confirm on payment\n    - user should be able to check the status of the product\n    - overselling or stock management must be correct non negotiable\n    - [Out of Scope] recommendation, logistic , copons , reviews writing,\n\n2. Non Functional Requirements\n     -  CAP Analysis\n             - Availability :\n                 - For Searching, catalog service   (stale price for 1 min is fine)\n                 - For Viewing the product            (session data, Redis)\n             - Consistancy \n                 - For stock management, order\n                 - For Payment and amount\n    - Latency \n                - product page < 200ms\n                - search result  <200ms\n\n    - Back of the envelop estimation\n            - DAU = 100 M\n            - Daily orders (10% of DAU) = 10 M\n            - Views per user = 10  ->  10 B reads/day\n            - Normal peak = 10x   |   Sale peak = 50x\n            - QPS\n                  - READ \n                          - peak    1 M      (10x)\n                          - sale    5 M      (50x)     \n                  - WRITE   avg   100\n                          - peak    1 K      (10x)\n                          - sale    5 K      (50x)   \n              Read : write = 1000 : 1 (Elastic search)\n            - STORAGE\n                  - Orders   10 M x 1 KB = 10 GB/day\n                                       = 3.6 TB/year\n                                       = ~36 TB / 10 yrs      \n                  - Product  100 M x 10 KB = 1 TB  TOTAL  (static catalog, not daily)\n                  - Images   100 M x 5 x 200 KB = 100 TB  \n             - HOT ROW\n              - Flash drop: 1 M users -> 10 K units -> 60 s\n                         = ~17 K QPS on ONE row     \n\n    3. Core Entities\n\n        - User \n        - Product \n        - Cart\n        - Order\n        - Checkouit\n\n4. API\n    1  GET  /v1/products/search?q={term}...\n            -> { products[], nextCursor }              cache 5m\n    \n    2 GET  /v1/products/{productId}\n            -> { id, title, ...}\n            availableQty = approximate, not truth      cache 1m\n    \n    3  POST    /v1/cart/items         { productId, qty }   -> { cart }\n    4  PATCH  /v1/cart/items/{id} { qty }              -> { cart }\n\n    5  POST /v1/checkout   => RESERVE                                \n           body { items[{productId, qty}] }\n           201  { orderId, status:PENDING, amount, expiresAt }\n           409  { error:OUT_OF_STOCK, productIds[] }\n    \n    6  POST /v1/orders/{orderId from Api 5}/confirm  =>   PAY\n       body { paymentToken }\n       200  { orderId, status:CONFIRMED }\n       410  { error:RESERVATION_EXPIRED }\n\n    7. GET:/v1/status/orderId",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Functional Requirements\n    - user should be able to search products based on name, description, title\n    - user should be able to view the details of a product .\n    - user should be able to select the product quantity and add to cart\n    - user should be able to reserve stock at checkout (hold N min) then confirm on payment\n    - user should be able to check the status of the product\n    - overselling or stock management must be correct non negotiable\n    - [Out of Scope] recommendation, logistic , copons , reviews writing,\n\n2. Non Functional Requirements\n     -  CAP Analysis\n             - Availability :\n                 - For Searching, catalog service   (stale price for 1 min is fine)\n                 - For Viewing the product            (session data, Redis)\n             - Consistancy \n                 - For stock management, order\n                 - For Payment and amount\n    - Latency \n                - product page < 200ms\n                - search result  <200ms\n\n    - Back of the envelop estimation\n            - DAU = 100 M\n            - Daily orders (10% of DAU) = 10 M\n            - Views per user = 10  ->  10 B reads/day\n            - Normal peak = 10x   |   Sale peak = 50x\n            - QPS\n                  - READ \n                          - peak    1 M      (10x)\n                          - sale    5 M      (50x)     \n                  - WRITE   avg   100\n                          - peak    1 K      (10x)\n                          - sale    5 K      (50x)   \n              Read : write = 1000 : 1 (Elastic search)\n            - STORAGE\n                  - Orders   10 M x 1 KB = 10 GB/day\n                                       = 3.6 TB/year\n                                       = ~36 TB / 10 yrs      \n                  - Product  100 M x 10 KB = 1 TB  TOTAL  (static catalog, not daily)\n                  - Images   100 M x 5 x 200 KB = 100 TB  \n             - HOT ROW\n              - Flash drop: 1 M users -> 10 K units -> 60 s\n                         = ~17 K QPS on ONE row     \n\n    3. Core Entities\n\n        - User \n        - Product \n        - Cart\n        - Order\n        - Checkouit\n\n4. API\n    1  GET  /v1/products/search?q={term}...\n            -> { products[], nextCursor }              cache 5m\n    \n    2 GET  /v1/products/{productId}\n            -> { id, title, ...}\n            availableQty = approximate, not truth      cache 1m\n    \n    3  POST    /v1/cart/items         { productId, qty }   -> { cart }\n    4  PATCH  /v1/cart/items/{id} { qty }              -> { cart }\n\n    5  POST /v1/checkout   => RESERVE                                \n           body { items[{productId, qty}] }\n           201  { orderId, status:PENDING, amount, expiresAt }\n           409  { error:OUT_OF_STOCK, productIds[] }\n    \n    6  POST /v1/orders/{orderId from Api 5}/confirm  =>   PAY\n       body { paymentToken }\n       200  { orderId, status:CONFIRMED }\n       410  { error:RESERVATION_EXPIRED }\n\n    7. GET:/v1/status/orderId",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
