    {
      "id": "4AhQlZl3DSP0T7JFYeV7B",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2785.1778817854465,
      "y": 4542.221650156667,
      "width": 379.44,
      "height": 315,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bPj",
      "seed": 1103414266,
      "version": 104,
      "versionNonce": 385504698,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786609743184,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "RULES THAT MAKE THIS CORRECT\n\n1  Redis is a filter, never the truth.\n2  No SELECT before UPDATE. The WHERE clause\n     IS the check, so there is no race window.\n3  Reserve at checkout, confirm at payment.\n     available -> reserved -> sold.\n4  A reservation is a DB row, not a cache key.\n     A Redis restart must not lose holds.\n5  Release order = DB first, Redis second.\n6  Nothing that decides stock or order state\n     goes through Kafka.\n7  One table, one owner. Only Inventory Service\n     writes the inventory table and redis.\n\nREMOVED FROM THE OLD DIAGRAM  (the bugs)\n\nx  Kafka -> Inventory DB      too late, oversell\nx  Kafka -> Redis counter     not Kafka's job\nx  Kafka -> Order DB            must be synchronous\nx  Checkout -> Inventory DB  skips the owner",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "RULES THAT MAKE THIS CORRECT\n\n1  Redis is a filter, never the truth.\n2  No SELECT before UPDATE. The WHERE clause\n     IS the check, so there is no race window.\n3  Reserve at checkout, confirm at payment.\n     available -> reserved -> sold.\n4  A reservation is a DB row, not a cache key.\n     A Redis restart must not lose holds.\n5  Release order = DB first, Redis second.\n6  Nothing that decides stock or order state\n     goes through Kafka.\n7  One table, one owner. Only Inventory Service\n     writes the inventory table and redis.\n\nREMOVED FROM THE OLD DIAGRAM  (the bugs)\n\nx  Kafka -> Inventory DB      too late, oversell\nx  Kafka -> Redis counter     not Kafka's job\nx  Kafka -> Order DB            must be synchronous\nx  Checkout -> Inventory DB  skips the owner",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "roundness": null
    },
